<h1>Settings</h1>

<h2>Backup client</h2>
<div class="panel" id="client">
  <p class="dim">Settings held by the Backblaze client itself, read and written through its own
  command line. The description under each one is the client's own wording, so it says what the
  Backblaze settings window says.</p>
  <p class="dim">Reading them starts a Windows process under Wine, so the values here are taken
  every few minutes rather than continuously. A change is written to the client's configuration
  file straight away, but whether a backup that is already running picks it up without the
  container being restarted has not been established. If a change does not seem to be taking
  effect, restart the container.</p>
  <div id="client-settings"><p class="dim">Reading the client.</p></div>
  <div id="client-err" class="err" hidden></div>
</div>

<h2>Notifications</h2>
<div class="panel" id="notify">
  <p class="dim">Get a message when something happens to the backup. Supported: ntfy, Pushbullet,
  Discord, Slack, Gotify, a plain JSON webhook (Home Assistant, your own script), or a JSON body
  you write yourself. An event is sent when it starts and again when it clears. Messages carry
  counts and reasons, not file names.</p>
  <div id="endpoints"></div>
  <button class="ghost" id="ep-add">Add endpoint</button>
  <h3>Events</h3>
  <div class="ev" id="events"></div>
  <label for="skipped-threshold">Files skipped: send from</label>
